# "As an additional cost to cast this spell, return a permanent you control to its owner's hand" (CR 118.8) needs a
# permanent of your own to return. Turn two Bot2 puts an Ornithopter on the battlefield: an opponent's permanent does not
# do. Turn three Bot1 casts a Black Lotus and taps it for {U}{U}{U}, which sacrifices it, so with the mana in the pool
# but no permanent left on Bot1's side the Fear is refused (a cast refused for want of mana would prove nothing).
# Turn five Bot1 plays an Island and casts a Mox Sapphire, taps both for exactly {1}{U} and casts the Fear, returning the
# tapped Mox to its hand as the cost: the pool is empty right after, the Fear has flying, and Bot2's Ornithopter stays.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Island
Mox Sapphire
Fear of Isolation
Island
Island
Island
Island
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Swamp x14

